1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:05,261
Same paper, same three questions: one set
goes to ChatGPT in the cloud,

2
00:00:05,261 --> 00:00:08,215
the other to an AI editor on your own
computer.

3
00:00:08,215 --> 00:00:10,728
Let's see how the two approaches differ.

4
00:00:11,567 --> 00:00:14,335
Here are all the prompts we used: three
questions,

5
00:00:14,335 --> 00:00:16,550
plus one sentence to save a Word report.

6
00:00:16,550 --> 00:00:19,262
For cross-checking, two more sentences to
Gemini.

7
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:28,245
The cloud approach: upload the PDF to the
web page, then ask one question at a time.

8
00:00:28,245 --> 00:00:30,993
The answers are thorough and cite the
paper.

9
00:00:32,033 --> 00:00:33,961
Finally, ask it for a Word report.

10
00:00:33,961 --> 00:00:35,379
That takes over a minute,

11
00:00:35,379 --> 00:00:38,725
and then you still have to download it and
open it in Word.

12
00:00:40,167 --> 00:00:43,654
The local approach: the paper is already
in your own folder.

13
00:00:43,654 --> 00:00:47,024
Open Claude Code in the editor and ask the
same questions.

14
00:00:48,067 --> 00:00:52,274
It finds the PDF in the folder on its own
and reads it before answering.

15
00:00:52,274 --> 00:00:55,954
For question two, it sorts all 100 test
questions into a table.

16
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:59,705
Then one sentence: save it as a Word
report.

17
00:00:59,705 --> 00:01:03,087
It loads the docx skill, writes code to
build the file,

18
00:01:03,087 --> 00:01:06,039
and even converts it to PDF to check the
layout.

19
00:01:07,100 --> 00:01:09,727
report.docx appears right in the same
folder,

20
00:01:09,727 --> 00:01:12,413
so you can open it in the editor and check
it.

21
00:01:13,467 --> 00:01:15,904
Then switch to Gemini to cross-check.

22
00:01:15,904 --> 00:01:19,989
It compares the report with the PDF item
by item: basic facts,

23
00:01:19,989 --> 00:01:24,336
question counts per domain, success and
failure cases. All correct.

24
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:28,953
It also flags paragraphs that are
background, not from the paper.

25
00:01:28,953 --> 00:01:30,483
After revising as suggested,

26
00:01:30,483 --> 00:01:34,145
those paragraphs are labeled as background
and saved as a new file.

27
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:39,435
Cloud: upload, ask, download; open a web
page and you're ready.

28
00:01:39,435 --> 00:01:42,702
Local: the AI reads and writes your files
directly,

29
00:01:42,702 --> 00:01:45,457
and another model can cross-check its
work.

30
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:50,374
Working locally is like moving the AI
Agent's brain onto your laptop.

31
00:01:50,374 --> 00:01:54,417
Right in your folder, it reads papers,
writes reports, and cross-checks,

32
00:01:54,417 --> 00:01:56,158
becoming your research partner.

